STOCHASTIC DARK ENERGY — OU + QNM KERNEL TEST
======================================================================
  Data source : DESI DR2 (arXiv:2503.14738)
  N bins      : 7
  z range     : [0.295, 2.330]
  WARNING: Results are PRELIMINARY with N=7 bins.
  95% CI on lag correlations: ≈ ±1.0 (non-significant).

─── MODEL COMPARISON ─────────────────────────────────────────
Model                              logL    ΔlogL   k       AIC       BIC
----------------------------------------------------------------------
ΛCDM (baseline)                  24.900    0.000   0       ref       ref
OU calibrated (θ=1.2)            21.821   -3.079   —         —         —
H0: OU free MLE                  24.900   -0.000   2   -45.799   -45.907
H1: QNM free MLE                 24.900   -0.000   3   -43.799   -43.961

─── BEST-FIT PARAMETERS ──────────────────────────────────────
  H0 (OU):  θ = 266.0518,  σ_X = 0.00005,  ω_R = 0 (fixed)
  H1 (QNM): θ = 0.0430,  σ_X = 0.00005,  ω_R = 6.9313
  H1 m_eff/H (de Sitter dispersion) = 7.0919

  Note: θ = 0.0430 ≈ 0: near-undamped oscillation. Likely a numerical artifact with N=7 bins, not a physical QNM. The dispersion relation gives m_eff/H = 7.092, but the near-zero decay rate is unphysical for de Sitter QNM.

─── MODEL SELECTION (AIC/BIC) ────────────────────────────────
  ΔAIC(H0 − H1) = -2.000  → H0 preferred  (|Δ| > 2 notable, > 6 strong)
  ΔBIC(H0 − H1) = -1.946  → H0 preferred  (|Δ| > 2 positive, > 6 strong)

  With N=7 bins, model selection is only indicative.
  More bins (e.g. Euclid DR1) are needed for a decisive test.

─── QNM CONSISTENCY: θ/ω_R RATIO ────────────────────────────
  θ/ω_R = 0.0430 / 6.9313 = 0.0062
  (This ratio = ω_I/ω_R constrains m_eff/H in de Sitter QNM.)
  Consistency check: if this ratio is inconsistent
  between DESI DR1, DR2, and Euclid → QNM kernel incoherent.

─── LINEARITY TEST: Δη vs Δx ────────────────────────────────
  Pearson r(Δη, Δx) over all 21 pairs = 0.998456
  ≈ Good linearity (r < 0.999). Consider 2nd-order correction in future versions.

─── LAG CORRELATIONS (whitened residuals) ────────────────────
  Note: 95% CI ≈ ±0.98 with N=7 bins. No lag is individually significant.

